  "description": "Rear dormer; three new windows to side elevation",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p style=&quot;margin-top: 5pt; margin-right: 0cm; margin-bottom: 0cm;&quot;&gt;The proposed rear dormer extension, by\r\nreason of its excessive bulk and massing would\r\nresult in an unduly obtrusive and incongruous addition that would poorly relate\r\nto the existing host property and the cottages in which No. 45 Waxwell Lane\r\nsits, detracting from the character properties in the Waxwell Lane Conservation\r\nArea. The rear dormer would thereby unacceptably harm the character of the\r\noriginal dwellinghouse and the visual amenities of the area, contrary to the\r\nhigh quality design aspirations set out in The National Planning Policy\r\nFramework (2024), policies D3 (D(1), D(11)) and HC1 of The London Plan (2021),\r\nPolicy CS1.B/D on the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policies DM1 and DM7 of the\r\nDevelopment Management Local Plans Policies (2013), the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010), and the&amp;nbsp;Waxwell Lane Conservation Area Appraisal and Management Strategy (2009).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
